<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Convention of Moss</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-norwegian-war">Swedish–Norwegian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Convention of Moss was the ceasefire agreement signed on 14 August 1814 at Moss, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Christiania</a>, that ended the brief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-norwegian-war">Swedish–Norwegian War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>'s regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-viii-of-denmark">Christian Frederik</a> agreed to abdicate, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> accepted the Norwegian constitution of 17 May 1814. It led to the union of Sweden and Norway, with Charles XIII elected king of Norway by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/storting">Storting</a> that November.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/convention-of-moss.jpg" alt="Convention of Moss" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Bjerketvedt Østby · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Konvensjonsg%C3%A5rden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
